# Duels anywhere + damage liability (absorb/liability.js, skills.toml [absorb.duel] / [absorb.liability]; owner 18/11/2026).
# `ttl liability expect ...` and `ttl econ expect ...` print "ttl: ..." when a value is wrong. A `ttl absorb simulate` line
# prints "absorb simulate: refused (...)" on purpose (these bots hold no uniques): it only ends the duel, through the same
# code path as the fatal blow, and settles the damage.
# Place: the Spirit Corridor, because it is void-safe for bots and holds the one build placed for tests (test_hut, corner
# 2498 63 -2, placed by builds.rcon, which runs first); the corridor spawn platform (0, 0) is in no build's box = "the
# wild". (A real duel in the corridor would not move a skill: exclude_dimensions; `simulate` skips that on purpose.)
# Inside the hut the block two above the bot's head (2499 66 -1) is interior air; the test puts stone there, "breaks" it
# with the test hook (`ttl liability testbreak`, the BlockEvents.broken path) and expects it back after settling.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] liability: TtlBotLiA vs TtlBotLiB opened in Test hut; TtlBotLiA is liable" and
# "[ttl] liability: TtlBotLiA charged 5 of 5 bronze for 1 blocks in Test hut (no nation)".
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLiA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotLiB
@sleep 2
ttl build expect test_hut placed
ttl absorb clear TtlBotLiA
ttl absorb clear TtlBotLiB
ttl liability clear
kubejs stages add TtlBotLiA ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotLiB ttl.life2
clear TtlBotLiA
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run forceload add 2496 -4 2504 4
# The wild: a duel there is nobody's business, nothing is recorded.
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run tp TtlBotLiA 0.5 65 0.5
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run tp TtlBotLiB 1.5 65 0.5
@sleep 1
ttl liability expect public TtlBotLiA no
execute as TtlBotLiA run ttl absorb duel TtlBotLiB
execute as TtlBotLiB run ttl absorb accept TtlBotLiA
ttl absorb expect pacts 1
ttl liability expect liable TtlBotLiA no
ttl absorb simulate TtlBotLiA TtlBotLiB duel
ttl absorb expect pacts 0
# A public place (a placed build): A challenges B inside the test hut, so A is liable for what the fight breaks there.
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run tp TtlBotLiA 2499.5 64 -0.5
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run tp TtlBotLiB 2501.5 64 0.5
@sleep 1
ttl liability where TtlBotLiA
ttl liability expect public TtlBotLiA yes
execute as TtlBotLiA run ttl absorb duel TtlBotLiB
execute as TtlBotLiB run ttl absorb accept TtlBotLiA
ttl liability expect liable TtlBotLiA yes
ttl liability expect liable TtlBotLiB yes
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run setblock 2499 66 -1 minecraft:stone
ttl liability testbreak TtlBotLiA
ttl liability expect changes 1
ttl liability expect above TtlBotLiA air
# The duel ends: the initiator A pays 5 bronze for the one block (a sink: the hut is no nation's land) and the block is
# put back on the next tick.
ttl econ give TtlBotLiA 100
ttl absorb simulate TtlBotLiA TtlBotLiB duel
ttl absorb expect pacts 0
ttl liability expect changes 0
ttl liability expect liable TtlBotLiA no
ttl econ expect TtlBotLiA balance 95
@sleep 1
ttl liability expect above TtlBotLiA stone
# Clean up.
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run setblock 2499 66 -1 minecraft:air
execute in ttl:spirit_corridor run forceload remove 2496 -4 2504 4
clear TtlBotLiA
ttl liability clear
ttl absorb clear TtlBotLiA
ttl absorb clear TtlBotLiB
kubejs stages remove TtlBotLiA ttl.life2
kubejs stages remove TtlBotLiB ttl.life2
ttlbot remove TtlBotLiA
ttlbot remove TtlBotLiB
